aces (API surface vs. support-process artifacts vs. integration promotion); no shared data structure or API endpoint is built by two epics. Parallel. |\n| E006 ∥ all Llama Stack epics | Rule 14 | Different repo (odh-dashboard), no shared build artifacts — the Dashboard works through Kubernetes CRs, not Llama Stack code. Parallel. |\n| E002..E006 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs last) | `docs-authoring` is blocked by every Implementation epic; docs describe what was built, including the remediated gaps, support posture, guardrails integration, and default enablement. |\n\nNo `konflux-onboarding`, `repo-onboarding`, or `license-validation` epics are\ngenerated: all components are in the platform inventory and already Konflux\nonboarded per architecture context.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 (assessment), E003 (gap closure) | The HLR's deliverable is the assessment producing the definitive GA scope (E001); closing the inventoried gaps is the follow-on work (E003), gated on E001's output. |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | E002 | Full coverage: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, tested upgrade path from last two TP releases. |\n| HLR-3 | P0 | E004 | SLO targets, backport policy, supported configuration matrix. |\n| HLR-4 | P1 | E005 | TrustyAI is a passive component (no code changes on its side); integration validation is an AC on E005. |\n| HLR-5 | P1 | E006 | Dashboard-owned; feature-flag/default change. |\n| HLR-6 | P2 | E007 | `bundled`? No — documentation is a distinct work-product stream and gets its own `docs-authoring` epic per Rule 11; its P0 priority comes from the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy `priority: Critical`), not from HLR-6's P2 label. |\n\nAll six HLRs are covered; none orphaned.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table,\n  Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, or NFRs. Teams inferred from\n  architecture c