k items.\n- Scale limits supported by the distribution are enforced and documented\n  (behavior at the limit is defined and tested).\n- Error handling across the published API surface is consistent and\n  actionable per the assessment's error-handling findings, verified by tests\n  covering the failure modes the assessment identified.\n- The remediation work is validated against the assessment report: no\n  must-fix gap remains open at completion.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: Delivers the closure of the gaps the GA-readiness\n  assessment inventories — the assessment (tracked separately) produces the\n  definitive GA scope; this epic closes the must-fix items in it.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39034,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cfc5b8eb1cc258d","agent_id":"ae0701df2f2f4057e","session_id":"a5ccff59-e83b-4c36-b1be-14c65ff6e583","uuid":"8dee9b24-25b2-4534-af31-a2da21366ab3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:49:11.909Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
