n can be configured with TrustyAI guardrails\n  without any experimental flag, using the distribution's supported\n  configuration surface.\n- An end-to-end validation demonstrates guardrails requests flowing from a\n  Llama Stack distribution to the TrustyAI service and behaving as\n  documented, including defined failure behavior when TrustyAI is\n  unavailable.\n- The TrustyAI team has signed off that the integration is supportable as a\n  supported combination (no open objections from the TrustyAI side).\n- The integration is covered by the distribution's automated tests so\n  regressions in the integration are caught.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. Full coverage\n  of this HLR; the documentation half is completed by the GA documentation\n  effort using this epic's validated integration.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40329,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cfc5b8eb1cc258d","agent_id":"ae0701df2f2f4057e","session_id":"a5ccff59-e83b-4c36-b1be-14c65ff6e583","uuid":"8f6d5b25-a1fc-47c4-98dc-133fff010c40","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:49:30.143Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
