 Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Llama Stack documentation meets GA standards as accepted by the docs\n  review: no TP-era caveats left on supported surfaces, supported usage is\n  accurately described.\n- Migration notes from TP exist and cover the differences between the last\n  two TP releases and GA, including deprecated API surfaces per the\n  deprecation policy.\n- Documentation for the supported TrustyAI guardrails integration and\n  default-enabled Dashboard management is published.\n- All content is technically reviewed against the implemented GA behavior\n  (API stability work, support posture, guardrails integration, Dashboard\n  enablement, gap remediation) by the owning engineers, with review sign-off\n  recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-6 (P2)**: Documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including\n  migration notes from TP. Full coverage of this HLR.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41592,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cfc5b8eb1cc258d","agent_id":"ae0701df2f2f4057e","session_id":"a5ccff59-e83b-4c36-b1be-14c65ff6e583","uuid":"289c2272-ac08-49eb-abad-f95c12f8451e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:49:49.473Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
