{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aee2a7a4078d6236","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack GA-readiness gap assessment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Llama Stack GA-Readiness Gap Assessment\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic delivers the definitive GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack,\n30\tinventorying the gaps between current Tech Preview quality and the GA bar\n31\tacross API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling. It\n32\tproduces the GA scope document that determines what the hardening work must\n33\tclose before graduation. This is the strategy's P0 foundation: until it lands,\n34\tthe size of the stability and hardening work is an estimate.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Systematically inventory gaps between current TP quality and the GA bar in\n39\t  four enumerated areas: API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error\n40\t  handling.\n41\t- Consolidate TP feedback scattered across support tickets into the gap\n42\t  inventory.\n43\t- Assess the current state of the Llama Stack distribution (API surface,\n44\t  LlamaStackDistribution CR lifecycle, provider integrations) against GA\n45\t  expectations for each area.\n46\t- Produce the definitive GA scope: a prioritized, gap-by-gap inventory with a\n47\t  recommended disposition for each gap (must-fix for GA, deferred, or\n48\t  already-met), forming the re-baselined scope for the hardening work that\n49\t  follows.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- The assessment report inventories gaps in all four areas (API stability,\n54\t  upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling) with each gap stated\n55\t  concretely enough to be scheduled as remediation work.\n56\t- Every gap entry carries a disposition: must-fix for GA, deferred with\n57\t  rationale, or already-met with evidence.\n58\t- TP feedback from support tickets is reflected in the inventory (each\n59\t  recurring TP complaint category maps to a gap entry or an explicit\n60\t  already-met/deferred disposition).\n61\t- The report identifies a definitive GA scope that the downstream hardening\n62\t  work can be re-baselined against, and is reviewed and accepted by the\n63\t  owning team.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: This epic delivers the GA-readiness assessment that\n68\t  inventories the gaps between current TP quality and the GA bar, producing\n69\t  the definitive GA scope.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a709942beeffec84","agent_id":"a7da80d2ef26e8f00","session_id":"a5ccff59-e83b-4c36-b1be-14c65ff6e583","uuid":"a66a6c81-705e-4445-b7e6-885bd5d5ae4c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:52:17.365Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aee2a7a4078d6236","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
