s epic must\n51\tfix. If the assessment finds no gaps beyond the explicitly required API\n52\tstability and support-posture work, this epic reduces to remediating only the\n53\tspecific findings; if it finds materially more, the epic is re-split along\n54\tgap-category lines (see the decomposition summary's health warnings).\n55\t\n56\t## Scope\n57\t\n58\t- Remediate the must-fix gaps identified by the GA-readiness assessment,\n59\t  including scale limits (documented and enforced limits for supported\n60\t  distribution sizes and workloads) and error handling (actionable, consistent\n61\t  error behavior across the published API surface).\n62\t- Re-baseline this epic's backlog against the assessment's gap inventory at\n63\t  the start of execution: each must-fix gap becomes a tracked work item here.\n64\t- Verify that remediated gaps meet the GA bar as stated by the assessment's\n65\t  dispositions.\n66\t\n67\t## Acceptance Criteria\n68\t\n69\t- Every gap the assessment dispositioned as must-fix for GA has a completed,\n70\t  verified remediation tracked in this epic's work items.\n71\t- Scale limits supported by the distribution are enforced and documented\n72\t  (behavior at the limit is defined and tested).\n73\t- Error handling across the published API surface is consistent and\n74\t  actionable per the assessment's error-handling findings, verified by tests\n75\t  covering the failure modes the assessment identified.\n76\t- The remediation work is validated against the assessment report: no\n77\t  must-fix gap remains open at completion.\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: Delivers the closure of the gaps the GA-readiness\n82\t  assessment inventories — the assessment (tracked separately) produces the\n83\t  definitive GA scope; this epic closes the must-fix items in it.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a709942beeffec84","agent_id":"a7da80d2ef26e8f00","session_id":"a5ccff59-e83b-4c36-b1be-14c65ff6e583","uuid":"e91fd31d-d725