{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a29c5378baf74841","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack API stability guarantees and tested TP upgrade path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Llama Stack API Stability Guarantees and Tested TP Upgrade Path\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic puts a stability guarantee on the published Llama Stack API surface:\n34\tversioned APIs, a documented deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path\n35\tfrom the last two Tech Preview releases. It delivers the HLR-2 portion of the\n36\tGA graduation — the commitment enterprise customers need before building\n37\tproduction GenAI applications on the component.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Introduce API versioning on the published Llama Stack API surface exposed\n42\t  by the distribution (OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the\n43\t  LlamaStackDistribution CRD surface as configured by the distribution).\n44\t- Define and document a deprecation policy: how API changes are versioned,\n45\t  announced, and retired, and what support window deprecated surfaces keep.\n46\t- Build and automate an upgrade-path test that verifies a distribution\n47\t  deployed on each of the last two TP releases upgrades to the GA release\n48\t  with documented, non-breaking behavior for the supported surface.\n49\t- Ensure the deprecation policy and versioning scheme are applied\n50\t  consistently across the published API surface.\n51\t- Scope boundary: this epic delivers only the enumerated stability machinery\n52\t  above. Any additional API-stability gap the GA-readiness assessment\n53\t  inventories is remediated in the assessment-findings remediation work, not\n54\t  here.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- The published API surface is versioned, and the versioning is visible and\n59\t  documented in the API surface the distribution exposes.\n60\t- A deprecation policy document exists stating versioning, announcement, and\n61\t  retirement rules for API changes, approved by the owning team.\n62\t- An automated upgrade-path test exists and passes for upgrades from each of\n63\t  the last two TP releases to the GA release, covering the supported\n64\t  configuration surface.\n65\t- No breaking change to the published, supported API surface is introduced\n66\t  without following the deprecation policy (verified by the upgrade-path\n67\t  test and API surface review).\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee —\n72\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last\n73\t  two TP releases. Full coverage of this HLR.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-963f9fd92f5abe9a","agent_id":"a8de30c105ee98776","session_id":"a5ccff59-e83b-4c36-b1be-14c65ff6e583","uuid":"a057fe7f-3750-4952-a761-4710425f67c8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:56:43.026Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a29c5378baf74841","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
