s epic must\n51\tfix. If the assessment finds no gaps beyond the explicitly required API\n52\tstability and support-posture work, this epic reduces to remediating only the\n53\tspecific findings; if it finds materially more, the epic is re-split along\n54\tgap-category lines (see the decomposition summary's health warnings).\n55\t\n56\t## Scope\n57\t\n58\t- Remediate the must-fix gaps identified by the GA-readiness assessment,\n59\t  including scale limits (documented and enforced limits for supported\n60\t  distribution sizes and workloads) and error handling (actionable, consistent\n61\t  error behavior across the published API surface).\n62\t- Ownership boundary with the API-stability work: the enumerated stability\n63\t  machinery — API versioning, the deprecation policy, and the automated\n64\t  upgrade-path test from the last two Tech Preview releases — is delivered by\n65\t  the API-stability epic. Any API-stability gap the assessment inventories\n66\t  beyond that enumerated machinery (for example, undocumented surface\n67\t  behavior or inconsistent error contracts on specific endpoints) is\n68\t  remediated in this epic, not there.\n69\t- Re-baseline this epic's backlog against the assessment's gap inventory at\n70\t  the start of execution: each must-fix gap becomes a tracked work item here.\n71\t- Verify that remediated gaps meet the GA bar as stated by the assessment's\n72\t  dispositions.\n73\t\n74\t## Acceptance Criteria\n75\t\n76\t- Every gap the assessment dispositioned as must-fix for GA has a completed,\n77\t  verified remediation tracked in this epic's work items.\n78\t- Scale limits supported by the distribution are enforced and documented\n79\t  (behavior at the limit is defined and tested).\n80\t- Error handling across the published API surface is consistent and\n81\t  actionable per the assessment's error-handling findings, verified by tests\n82\t  covering the failure modes the assessment identified.\n83\t- The remediation work is validated against the assessment report: no\n84\t  must-fix gap remains open at completion.\n85\t\n86\t## HLR Traceability\n87\t\n88\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: Delivers the closure of the gaps the GA-readiness\n89\t  assessment inventories — the assessment (tracked separately) produces the\n90\t  definitive GA scope; this epic closes the must-fix items in it.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-963f9fd92f5abe9a","agent_id":"a8de30c105ee98776","session_id":"a5ccff59-e83b-4c36-b1be-14c65ff6e583","uuid":"a519bdd3-7143-4a38-9999-38daf8fb044c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:56:43.847Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-873171fd81209cbe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
