{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca9b9233748ac19","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E005\n3\ttitle: Promote TrustyAI guardrails to a supported integration in Llama Stack distributions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Promote TrustyAI Guardrails to a Supported Integration in Llama Stack Distributions\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic promotes Llama Stack's TrustyAI safety-guardrails integration from\n34\tan experimental flag to a supported, documented integration available in GA\n35\tLlama Stack distributions. TrustyAI itself is already a Stable (GA) platform\n36\tcomponent providing guardrails services; the change is on the Llama Stack\n37\tdistribution side — making the integration a first-class supported option\n38\trather than an experimental opt-in — and validating it jointly with the\n39\tTrustyAI service.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Remove the experimental status of the TrustyAI guardrails integration in\n44\t  Llama Stack distributions: the integration is available and supported in\n45\t  GA distributions without an experimental opt-in flag.\n46\t- Wire the integration so it follows the distribution's established provider/\n47\t  integration configuration patterns rather than an experimental side\n48\t  channel.\n49\t- Validate the integration end-to-end with the TrustyAI service: guardrails\n50\t  requests from a Llama Stack distribution are served by TrustyAI as\n51\t  documented, with defined behavior when the TrustyAI service is unavailable.\n52\t- Obtain TrustyAI-team sign-off that the integration is supportable as a\n53\t  supported combination (TrustyAI is owned by a separate team; the\n54\t  integration must be validated from both sides).\n55\t- Document the integration's supported status as part of the GA documentation\n56\t  effort (content delivered there; this epic supplies the validated\n57\t  integration and the technical facts).\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- A GA Llama Stack distribution can be configured with TrustyAI guardrails\n62\t  without any experimental flag, using the distribution's supported\n63\t  configuration surface.\n64\t- An end-to-end validation demonstrates guardrails requests flowing from a\n65\t  Llama Stack distribution to the TrustyAI service and behaving as\n66\t  documented, including defined failure behavior when TrustyAI is\n67\t  unavailable.\n68\t- The TrustyAI team has signed off that the integration is supportable as a\n69\t  supported combination (no open objections from the TrustyAI side).\n70\t- The integration is covered by the distribution's automated tests so\n71\t  regressions in the integration are caught.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n76\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. Full coverage\n77\t  of this HLR; the documentation half is completed by the GA documentation\n78\t  effort using this epic's validated integration.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-963f9fd92f5abe9a","agent_id":"a8de30c105ee98776","session_id":"a5ccff59-e83b-4c36-b1be-14c65ff6e583","uuid":"2e6b4502-ef90-4dba-9b4e-860b2eb3cf77","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:56:48.206Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca9b9233748ac19","permission_decision":{"decisio